    "explanation": "Article 266 establishes three critical fiscal structures: (1) The Consolidated Fund of India — all government revenues and loans flow into this fund, and no money can be withdrawn except with parliamentary appropriation; (2) The Public Account of India — money held by the government in trust (provident funds, small savings, deposits) goes here; (3) Similarly for each State. The distinction between Consolidated Fund (requires parliamentary vote) and Public Account (does not require vote) is fundamental to parliamentary control over public finances.",
