    "explanation": "Article 270 establishes the divisible pool — the pot of central taxes that is shared with states. The Finance Commission recommends the share of states in this pool (currently 41% as per the 15th Finance Commission for 2021-26). This is the primary mechanism for vertical devolution — transferring revenue from the centre to the states. The horizontal distribution (how much each state gets) is based on factors like population, per capita income, area, forest cover, and demographic performance.",
