    "explanation": "Article 271 permits Parliament to levy surcharges on taxes that would otherwise be shared with States. Crucially, surcharge proceeds are NOT part of the divisible pool — they go entirely to the Centre. This has been controversial because increasing reliance on cesses and surcharges effectively reduces States' share of central tax revenue.",
