    "part": "PART XII — FINANCE, PROPERTY, CONTRACTS, AND SUITS",
    "title": "Article 293: Borrowing by States",
    "definition": "(1) States may borrow within India upon the security of the State Consolidated Fund within limits fixed by the State Legislature. (2) The Union may make loans to States. (3) If a State has outstanding Union loans, it cannot raise further loans without central consent. (4) The Union may impose conditions on such consent.",
    "explanation": "Article 293 governs State borrowing — States can borrow within India (not abroad) upon the security of the State Consolidated Fund. If a State has outstanding loans from the Centre, it cannot raise further borrowing without Central consent. This gives the Centre significant control over State finances and fiscal discipline. The FRBM framework at the State level also restricts borrowing.",
