    "title": "Article 294: Succession to property, assets, rights, liabilities, and obligations in certain cases",
    "definition": "On the commencement of the Constitution, property, assets, rights, liabilities, and obligations of the Dominion and of Provinces devolved in the manner laid down by the article.",
    "explanation": "Article 294 was a foundational succession clause for the transition from colonial to constitutional governance.",
